&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Group Head of Membership &amp;amp; Loyalty (TakealotMORE)&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us. We offer a market-related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group Head of TakealotMORE is responsible for defining and driving the strategic vision, growth, and operational efficiency of TakealotMORE, the subscription loyalty program for the Takealot Group. The role ensures the successful alignment of loyalty initiatives with the broader customer, marketing, and business strategies, leveraging data and insights to enhance customer experience, value delivery, and program sustainability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position reports to the Group Executive: Customer &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Vision &amp;amp; Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the TakealotMORE strategy, aligning with the Group’s customer-centric objectives to drive multi-platform adoption, retention, and revenue growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the long-term vision for TakealotMORE, incorporating innovative features, partnerships, and customer benefits to maximise loyalty and lifetime value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Growth &amp;amp; Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define initiatives to drive subscription growth, improving member retention rates, purchase frequency, and cross-platform engagement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise TakealotMORE benefits and offerings to ensure long-term value and attractiveness for current and potential subscribers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the TALMORE brand &amp;amp; positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead brand and marketing strategies unique to TakealotMORE, working collaboratively with BU-level marketing, CRM, and customer insights teams for effective execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the planning, development, and execution of comprehensive, data-driven strategies and marketing campaigns across multiple channels to boost visibility, drive subscription sign-ups, enhance customer engagement, and improve retention for TakealotMORE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Collaboration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product and Engineering teams to enhance the user experience; drive seamless integration of loyalty features into platforms such as &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across internal teams (e.g., Customer Analytics, Customer &amp;amp; Business Support) to leverage insights for program refinement and personalisation efforts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, establish and manage strategic partnerships with third-party vendors and service providers to enhance the loyalty program&#39;s attractiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional collaboration: Collaboration with various teams such as Marketing, Operations, Customer Service, Retail, Finance, Product, and Engineering is essential. The Head of TakealotMORE needs to work closely with these teams to align strategies and achieve overall success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P&amp;amp;L Ownership &amp;amp; Metrics Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the Profit &amp;amp; Loss (P&amp;amp;L) of TakealotMORE by monitoring and optimising program economics to strike a balance between customer satisfaction, value delivery, operational efficiency, profitability, and long-term sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor KPIs, including subscription growth rates, net promoter scores (NPS), revenue contributions, and churn reduction, to inform program improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Operational Effectiveness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the evolution of the loyalty program, incorporating emerging technologies such as AI and machine learning into customer segmentation, campaign optimisation, and program enhancements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously refine operational efficiencies, focusing on seamless enrolment, faster resolution times, and automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up-to-date with industry best practices in the subscription loyalty sector to ensure that the strategies remain cutting-edge and competitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth in subscription sign-up rates, retention rates, and active membership base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduction in churn and improvement of the subscriber retention rate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Purchase frequency and order value uplift for subscribers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loyalty program profitability and cost per retained subscriber.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced profitability and contribution margin from the loyalty program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased cross-platform usage and engagement across &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective delivery of marketing campaigns and partnerships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent improvement in customer satisfaction, NPS, and program-specific metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Insights Leadership – Align loyalty strategy with customer engagement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D – Drive program adoption and cross-platform benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Unit Marketing – Develop acquisition, retention, and promotional campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product &amp;amp; Technology – Enhance platform capabilities for loyalty integration and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Service and Experience teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Insights &amp;amp; Experience – Leverage insights for segmentation, personalisation, and targeted engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External Partners – Negotiate and integrate third-party loyalty benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Marketing, or a related field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An MBA or related advanced degree is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 - 10 years of commercial experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to senior managers and the C-suite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the tech sector / building a product from the ground up - advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling cross-functional collaboration within large matrix organisations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of P&amp;amp;L management and delivering revenue-enhancing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to inspire, lead, and navigate cross-functional teams to drive results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Thinking: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong capability to conceptualise and execute forward-looking initiatives in subscription-based loyalty management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Decision Making&lt;/strong&gt;: Expertise in using data analytics to interpret customer behaviour and adjust strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to initiate and implement technology-driven improvements like AI-based segmentation and personalisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at stakeholder alignment with a solutions-focused approach to cross-departmental coordination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, knowledge &amp;amp; abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about Takealot Group, its brands, and customers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker; able to build a vision for the vertical and translate this vision into product design and operational plans&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solutions-oriented executor; can-do attitude; self-motivated&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Data Analysis, manipulation, and Reporting Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Problem-Solving Skills and Solutions-Oriented Mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical: uses data to inform decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with change&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trustworthy and ethical&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced skills in the Google Suite, Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer- centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e- commerce company in Africa.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; We are short on ego and high on output.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; We are doers and not only thinkers, it&#39;s all in the execution after all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; We love what we do and what we are creating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We seek to employ an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;who&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;is &lt;/span&gt;Smart, has Integrity,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;and &lt;/span&gt;is Hardworking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you meet the above, you are an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind, &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;so come and join us! &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Takealot Group is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage applicants from previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities to apply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly accomplished &lt;strong&gt;Head of Corporate Communications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Corporate Affairs team in &lt;strong&gt;Cape Town&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us. We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the&lt;strong&gt; Group Executive: Public Affairs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate narrative and reputation strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead the Takealot Group corporate communications and reputation strategy, aligned to business strategy, the Group&amp;amp;#39;s South African identity, economic contribution, innovation agenda and social impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain a clear messaging architecture, approved proof points and corporate narrative that can be used consistently across Group functions and business units without diluting their distinct customer brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position the Group credibly on the issues that shape its licence to grow: e-commerce and the digital economy, entrepreneurship and localisation, employment and platform work, logistics innovation, consumer trust and inclusive growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate the strategy into a prioritised annual communications plan linked to material reputation risks, policy priorities, business milestones and opportunities for proactive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media relations, executive communications and thought leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Group-level relationships with business, political, technology, labour, consumer and general news media, building a proactive programme rather than a predominantly reactive press office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and prepare the Group CEO and designated executives for interviews, speeches, opinion pieces, panels and other high-value platforms; ensure executive visibility is purposeful and tied to strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead communications for Group results, material corporate announcements, partnerships and strategic milestones in coordination with Finance, Legal, Naspers/Prosus and the relevant business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set media-response and spokesperson protocols, oversee high-risk media enquiries and ensure the Group and BU teams communicate accurately, consistently and at appropriate speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Issu&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;es, crisis and reputation risk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an active reputation and issues register linked to Public Policy, Risk, Legal and operational risk processes, identifying emerging narratives before they become material reputation events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scenario plans, holding statements, key messages, escalation paths and spokesperson arrangements for priority risks, including driver and labour issues, community tension, consumer or product-safety concerns, regulatory scrutiny, technology incidents and operational disruption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the communications response during Group-level crises and coordinate relevant BU, Legal, Risk, Operations, Customer and executive stakeholders around a single verified position and clear decision rights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Public policy, stakeholder and social impact communication&lt;/strong&gt;s&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Public Policy and Stakeholder Relations to translate complex policy positions into clear public narratives without pre-empting the accountable advocacy or negotiating mandate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build communications strategies around priority issues such as the future of platform work and the Third Way, fair e-commerce competition and customs/VAT parity, consumer protection, localisation, driver ecosystem sustainability and digital economic inclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the narrative for the Takealot Township Economy Initiative (TTEI) and broader social impact agenda, connecting driver development, marketplace SMEs, township and rural inclusion, franchisee development and skills programmes to measurable economic contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Social Impact, Sustainability, Finance and programme owners to ensure public claims are evidence-based, balanced and auditable; turn verified data and human stories into credible stakeholder and media content without overclaiming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group and business-unit communications governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and embed the operating model, decision rights and escalation protocols between Group Corporate Communications and the CMOs of takealot.com, Mr D and TFS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convene a regular Group communications forum to align major announcements, emerging issues, executive visibility and narrative priorities while preserving BU ownership of consumer and commercial marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retain final accountability for the Group&amp;amp;#39;s institutional position and corporate reputation. The relevant CMO retains final accountability for customer brand and commercial execution; major launches, partnerships, incidents and public-interest campaigns are coordinated jointly where the two intersect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a single source of truth for approved corporate facts, messages, policy positions and proof points, with clear approval routes for corporate statements, media responses and reputation-sensitive communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reputation intelligence, capability and delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a decision-useful reputation intelligence capability covering media, stakeholder sentiment, message penetration, misinformation, emerging issues, competitor narratives and material shifts in the external environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure what matters: quality and relevance of coverage, message pull-through, stakeholder understanding and trust, executive credibility, issue preparedness and response effectiveness. Do not rely on advertising-value equivalency or volume alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead the corporate communications team and agency model, manage approved budgets and develop strong capability in writing, media relations, issues management, research, executive communications and rapid response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled monitoring, research, drafting and scenario preparation to improve speed and coverage while retaining human judgement, source verification, confidentiality, editorial accountability and the required Legal or executive approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An Honours degree in Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, Corporate Affairs, Business, Political Science, Public Policy, Law, Economics or a related field. A relevant master&#39;s degree is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 12 years experience in corporate communications, reputation management, strategic communications, public affairs or journalism in a complex, high-profile or regulated organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years at senior leadership level, advising CEOs, executive committees or boards and leading teams, agencies and budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record across corporate narrative, media relations, executive communications and issues or crisis management, including coordination across brands or business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating sensitive policy, regulatory or societal issues, influencing without direct authority and making sound decisions under pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic judgement; corporate storytelling; commercial,&amp;nbsp;political and societal acumen; strong issues and crisis&amp;nbsp;leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive influence, cross-functional collaboration and the ability to create alignment without unnecessarily centralising BU accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity, discretion, courage and calm under pressure; able to challenge constructively, move at pace and know when the Group should not speak.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the South African media,&amp;nbsp;political, regulatory and socioeconomic environment and&amp;nbsp;the reputation dynamics facing digital businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing, editing, briefing and verbal communication; able to simplify complex business, policy and technical issues accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage Group/BU brand architecture: protect a coherent institutional position while enabling distinct customer brands and commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn policy, social-impact and economic-contribution evidence into credible narratives without overclaiming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability in reputation measurement, media intelligence, executive positioning, crisis simulation and communications governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible use of AI for monitoring, research and drafting, with source verification, confidentiality and human editorial accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;Mr%20D&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;We laugh hard, work harder, and take full ownership of our wins (and learning moments!)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teamwork makes the dream work – we&#39;re solution-seekers who thrive on collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; href=&quot;Mr%20D&quot;&gt;Got feedback? Bring it on! We&#39;re always hungry for fresh ideas and honest input&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot; href=&quot;Mr%20D&quot;&gt;Ego? We checked that at the door. Results? Now we&#39;re talking!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;so come and join us! &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Takealot Group is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities, to apply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly accomplished &lt;strong&gt;Head: Driver Experience and Future of Work&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our Corporate Affairs team in &lt;strong&gt;Cape Town&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us. We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head: Driver Experience and Future of Work, this role is the Group steward of the experience, working conditions, voice and wellbeing of&amp;nbsp;independent delivery drivers participating across the Takealot Group&amp;nbsp;ecosystem. The role will build the strategic capability and practical&amp;nbsp;proof points required to ensure that flexibility and independence are&amp;nbsp;reinforced by fair economic opportunity, transparency, meaningful&amp;nbsp;voice, safety, development and appropriate social protection. It&amp;nbsp;operates independently of driver recruitment and day-to-day driver&amp;nbsp;operations, translating driver evidence into systemic improvements&amp;nbsp;across the Group and strengthening Takealot Group’s leadership on&amp;nbsp;the future of platform-enabled work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the&lt;strong&gt; Group Executive: Public Affairs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driver Experience and Working Conditions &lt;/strong&gt;- Develop and own a Group-wide Driver Experience and Future of Work strategy, defining the standards, principles and measures that should shape the driver experience from onboarding and activation through participation, support, development, retention and exit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable Driver Proposition &lt;/strong&gt;- Shape a clear driver value proposition&amp;nbsp;that balances flexibility and autonomy with fair economic opportunity,&amp;nbsp;dignity and recognition, transparency, development, safety and&amp;nbsp;appropriate protections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driver Voice and Social Dialogue&lt;/strong&gt; - Build a structured architecture for&amp;nbsp;driver voice, including regional listening, driver forums, working groups,&lt;br&gt;surveys and engagement with recognized driver leaders, associations&amp;nbsp;and other representative structures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Governance&lt;/strong&gt; - Own and run the monthly Group Driver Wellbeing Forum, elevating it into a strategic Driver Experience and Future of Work governance mechanism with a common evidence base, clear priorities, accountable owners and tracked outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driver Insights and Economics&lt;/strong&gt; - Build the Group’s authoritative evidence base on driver experience and real driver economics, including gross and net earnings, participation costs, utilisation, earnings variability, supply-demand dynamics, attrition and reasons for exit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transparency, Fairness and Remedy &lt;/strong&gt;- Establish Group principles and&amp;nbsp;standards for the driver experience of earnings and incentives,&amp;nbsp;deductions, performance measures, access to opportunities, account&amp;nbsp;restrictions, complaints, appeals, grievance escalation and fair treatment,&amp;nbsp;while leaving operational execution with accountable business owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing and Social Protection &lt;/strong&gt;- Develop the Group strategy for driver&amp;nbsp;wellbeing and appropriate portable protections, including accident and&amp;nbsp;insurance cover, health and psychosocial support, financial wellbeing,&amp;nbsp;savings and resilience, emergency support and other fit-for-purpose&amp;nbsp;protections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety and Vision Zero&lt;/strong&gt; - Lead the strategic driver-safety agenda in&amp;nbsp;partnership with Operations, Risk and franchisees, using data and root-cause analysis to reduce road-safety, crime, fatigue and serious-incident&amp;nbsp;risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development and Economic Mobility&lt;/strong&gt; - Partner with Driver Programmes and Social Impact on skills, learning, asset access, financial capability, entrepreneurship and other pathways that can improve drivers’ longer-term economic mobility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driver-Centred Culture&lt;/strong&gt; - Build greater organisational understanding of the lived experience of drivers through direct engagement, immersion and&amp;nbsp;insight, and champion dignity, respect and driver-centred decision-making&amp;nbsp;across the Group and partner ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Future of Work and Public Policy &lt;/strong&gt;— Translate driver evidence and&amp;nbsp;emerging regulatory developments into practical operating and policy&lt;br&gt;recommendations, strengthening the Group’s ability to demonstrate that&amp;nbsp;flexibility, independence and meaningful protection can coexist in&amp;nbsp;practice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Influence&lt;/strong&gt; — Drive systemic improvements through the&amp;nbsp;accountable business functions without assuming ownership of driver&amp;nbsp;recruitment, day-to-day driver operations or franchisee management.&amp;nbsp;Recruitment remains within TFS; driver operations and franchisee&amp;nbsp;management remain within the existing operational structures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A relevant Honours degree in Business, Economics, Public Policy,&amp;nbsp;Behavioural Science, Social Sciences, Industrial Psychology,&amp;nbsp;Development Studies, Labour Relations or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A relevant postgraduate qualification is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years’ relevant professional experience across several of the&amp;nbsp;following areas: worker or customer experience, platform/gig economy,&amp;nbsp;future of work, workforce strategy, social impact, labour-market&amp;nbsp;programmes, human-centred design, social protection, financial inclusion,&amp;nbsp;public policy or large-scale programme leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years’ experience operating at senior management level or&amp;nbsp;leading complex, enterprise-wide programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience influencing senior stakeholders and delivering&amp;nbsp;outcomes across functions without relying on direct line authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, logistics, last-mile delivery, mobility, food&amp;nbsp;delivery, ride-hailing or another platform-enabled environment is&amp;nbsp;advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
