&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission, should you choose to accept it:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the roadmap for features and services that power the on-demand logistics execution platform, supporting a network of 20,000 last-mile drivers operating in the network. This includes innovating and improving the back-end systems that enable seamless and scalable delivery execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering, design, operations, and executive teams to enhance driver and logistics systems. Collaborate with drivers and logistics stakeholders to ensure the product meets both operational and customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs into actionable and measurable projects; partner with business owners to understand their challenges and priorities, to translate these into initiatives that improve the on-demand delivery experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement by evolving product management practices to suit the fast-paced, dynamic nature of on-demand logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor key metrics (e.g., delivery times, driver utilization, cost per delivery) to inform product decisions. Use data to create compelling business cases for prioritizing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will analyse and understand project scope and core objectives through requirements workshops with stakeholders to define business requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct workshops with stakeholders to elicit detailed functional requirements. Document these requirements (OKR &amp;amp; BRS) for engineering teams to create technical specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with technical lead and subject matter experts to establish the technical vision and analyse trade-offs between usability and performance needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with technical leads and subject matter experts to align on the technical vision, balancing the operational trade-offs with usability, scalability, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional teams, including engineers, BI analysts, and UI designers, to deliver projects on time and within scope. Track project progress from concept to release, ensuring alignment with business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve appropriate Product Management practices for a responsive, dynamic environment to foster cost-effective execution to commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with QA teams to review test plans and scripts, ensuring comprehensive coverage and high-quality product releases. Perform user acceptance testing to validate functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management by setting timelines, driving project schedules and leading cross-functional development teams from design through to release. This includes monitoring for slippage and/or updating timelines and adjusting for changing scopes of work or considering mitigation options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand your target “customer” - assess both drivers and end-users to ensure products deliver a seamless, efficient, and transparent experience..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing user acceptance testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Bachelor&#39;s Degree or Advanced Diploma (Information Systems/Computer Science/Engineering/Commerce) with at least 4 years of experience in product management, business analysis, or a related role, preferably driving large, company-wide initiatives (through projects or responsibilities)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an agile/iterative project management and development environment is beneficial&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in logistics, on-demand delivery platforms, or e-commerce is highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
